href":"#protocol-actiondesc","id":"footnote-reference-7"}]},"."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Alternatives"],"id":"alternatives"},{"tag":"p","children":["The original version of ZIP-225 included Sprout-related fields ","nJoinSplit",", ","vJoinSplit",", ","joinSplitPubKey",", and ","joinSplitSig"," in the V5 transaction format. The Electric Coin Company and Zcash Foundation teams have elected to remove these fields from the V5 transaction format as part of the continuing process of deprecation of the Sprout shielded pool. As a consequence of these fields being removed:"]},{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["This effectively prohibits migration transactions that would directly move funds from the Sprout pool to the Orchard pool. Sprout -> Transparent and Sprout -> Sapling migration transactions will still be supported when using the V4 transaction format."]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["Removing these fields reduces the complexity of the NU5 upgrade in the following ways:"]},{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["V5 parsing and serialization code does not need to take these fields into account."]}]},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["ZIP 244 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["7"],"href":"#zip-0244","id":"footnote-reference-8"}]}," transaction identifier, signature hash, and authorizing data commitment computations are simplified by excluding consideration of these fields."]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["Removal of these fields means that that in the future, removing the support for the V4 transaction format will also effectively end support for Sprout transactions on the Zcash network, though it might be possible to restore limited support for migration via a future ZIP 222 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["6"],"href":"#zip-0222","id":"footnote-reference-9"}]}," extension or by other means not yet determined."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The original definitions for the transaction fields that have been removed are:"]},{"tag":"table","children":[{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"strong","children":["Sprout Transaction Fields"]}]}],"colspan":4}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["varies"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["nJoinSplit"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["compactSize"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["The number of JoinSplit descriptions in ","vJoinSplit","."]}]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["1698 * nJoinSplit"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["vJoinSplit"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["JSDescriptionGroth16[nJoinSplit]"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["A sequence of JoinSplit descriptions using Groth16 proofs, encoded per §7.2 ‘JoinSplit Description Encoding and Consensus’."]}]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["32"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["joinSplitPubKey"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["byte[32]"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["An encoding of a JoinSplitSig public validating key."]}]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["64"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["joinSplitSig"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["byte[64]"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["A signature on a prefix of the transaction encoding, to be verfied using joinSplitPubKey as specified in §4.11 ‘Non-malleability (Sprout)’."]}]}]}]}]},{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["The ","joinSplitPubKey"," and ","joinSplitSig"," fields were specified to be present if and only if ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚗"]},{"tag":"